{
  "version": 271,
  "released": "2026-08-31",
  "changelog": "v271: EVENT IDENTITY, PHASE I2b — CONTAINERS FIRST. I0-I3 taught the substrate SAMENESS, and the first real-vault dry run bound nothing. The owner read that correctly as an emphasis error: life is a tree — life, age frames, big named spans (Etherfuse 2021 to now), moments inside them — and most of a vault's tellings are MEMBERS of a stretch somebody lived, not duplicates of each other. Collection outranks dedup. The controlling design is lifehug-platform `docs/design/event-identity.md` v4.2, amendment 12b (rulings 1, 2, 5, 6, 7) and the 13.5 promises; this repo's summary is ADR 0031, updated to say I2b shipped.\n\nTHE ENTITY SIGNAL. A roster-resolved same entity — v221's own resolution machinery, the one that knows Betty-Jo is Betty Jo, pointed at organizations and named stretches as well as people — is now one independent signal, in retrieval (a seventh blocking signal, one point of plausibility) and in R1's condition 4. It closes the gap the founder's dry run found: a recorder telling keeps the name in `subject_mention` (\"Etherfuse\", started, 2022-05) while a classifier telling keeps it inside a sentence (\"Started Etherfuse\"), so the two shared nothing but a word. The roster is what recognizes the word as an entity this life contains, and recognition is evidence a string match is not — a shared token that resolves to nobody still yields nothing. ONE FACT, ONE SIGNAL: an entity another signal already counted (a shared participant, a shared place) is SUBTRACTED before the entities are scored, which is #300's rule generalized after this rung's own first run bound three pairs on `place, entity` where the entity WAS the place. R1's floor is unchanged at two independent non-label signals, and the entity signal has never bound anything on its own.\n\nTHE CONTAINMENT RUNG, FOR EXACTLY TWO RULE IDS. A new module, `system/episode_containers.py`, mints deterministic `part_of` records under `entity_span` (the telling shares a resolved entity with a container whose span came from the person's own words, and its date is inside that span or absent) and `question_context` (the answer was given to a question that TARGETED the container — a fact about what was asked, not an inference from what was said). C2's origin gate (`event_identity.validate_event_identity`) widens for `part_of` exactly that far and refuses every third rule id by name; I2's language rung (\"during Etherfuse\", parsed out of prose) guesses and still files as a proposal.\n\nWHAT A CONTAINER IS, IN THE PERSON'S OWN WORDS. Not any dated telling: a telling that OPENS A SPAN. A `started` claim at stated basis opens one, an `ended` claim closes it, a stated value that is itself a proper range IS one — so \"May 2022 - Present\" reads as an open-ended stretch rather than as a month, and a point-dated moment (a birth, an email) is never a container. Its ENTITIES come from what it is ABOUT (its subject mentions), so a job telling that mentions college does not become the college. A container's id is minted from the container ALONE, because an id that digested its members would re-key every time somebody joined and orphan every record already filed against it.\n\nA MEMBERSHIP IS A RECEIPT, NOT A BOUND. C2's `validate_identity_set` had read section 5.4's telling-level refusal as covering `part_of` while C3's `active_binding_index` had always read it narrowly — two halves of one contract disagreeing in silence since I0. Section 13.5 settles it: *a member of two containers renders in both with one primary display decision*, the eras paradigm arriving here intact. A telling still belongs to at most ONE episode by `same` — that is the identity collapse the whole floor protects — and containment is not identity. The fold still refuses to CHOOSE: two containing episodes give the member no possible outer range at all, because picking one would be an answer nobody gave.\n\nAUTHORITY IS THE HOST'S FLAG, AND IT TOUCHES ONE FIELD. `bind-episodes --containment-authority {proposed,applied}` (default `proposed`) chooses `origin` and nothing else. `origin` is outside `IDENTITY_IDENTITY_KEYS`, so both authorities mint the SAME `identity_id`, the same rule id, the same evidence and the same directory under `state/` — the only consequence is which side of `GROUPING_ORIGINS` the record lands on, which is to say whether the fold publishes it as `containments` or as `proposed_links`. A host flips it when the drag-out gesture that removes a wrong placement is live, and nothing is re-keyed.\n\nTHE RECORDER'S STAMP RIDES THE SOURCE. `TemporalClaim` gains no field (section 9 holds): `temporal_store.promote_conversational_source` understands one additive metadata key, `question_context`, written to the promoted source's own frontmatter and outside `PROMOTION_IDENTITY_KEYS`, and `episode_binder.read_question_contexts` hands the binder a `{telling_ref: container}` map off the vault. A stamp that names no container this run knows is a NAMED diagnostic, never a placement into whatever happened to be nearby.\n\nTHE DRY RUN REPORTS CONTAINMENTS PER CONTAINER, with the rule and the reason for every member, and counts named for what they count (`containers`, `containment_members`, `containment_tellings`, `containment_by_rule`, `unresolved_question_contexts`). The rung runs wherever `plan()` runs — the weekly maintenance step, an answer-time pass and an operator run — and never inside `compile`; the maintenance seat is still a dry run by construction.\n\nON THE FOUNDER'S OWN VAULT (a frozen clone, 883 tellings): the run that bound nothing now finds THREE containers and places 48 memberships over 27 tellings — the Etherfuse tellings collect under `Etherfuse (after May 2022)` and under `the idea for Etherfuse (after 2021)`, with `Joy Labs (November 2018–January 2021)` beside them. A telling dated 1999 that names Etherfuse is left for the person rather than moved to fit.\n\nPROVEN TO FIRE. Twenty mutations were applied one at a time to a copy of this build and every one was caught: the origin gate always saying yes; a third rule id joining the closed widening; an unknown authority silently becoming proposed; the entity signal counting a fact another signal already counted; a three-letter roster key passing as a name; a point-dated moment becoming a container; a `started` claim no longer opening a span; \"inside\" degrading to \"compatible\"; a container named by everything it mentions; a container id digesting its members; the entity rung outranking the question context; an unresolvable stamp guessed at, or not reported at all; a container placed inside itself; the block losing its order; two `part_of` receipts refused again; the entity signal leaving retrieval or condition 4; the stamp no longer riding the source frontmatter; and the authority flag no longer choosing the origin.",
